  offerDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Now that you've seen the new material, let's look at today's <b><#E09500>contract</color></b>.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - The bridge must safely carry the <b><#E09500>Vehicle</color></b> crossing one
      after another.
    - This time, the road alone will not be enough.
    - You'll reinforce it using the <b><#E09500>Wood Beams</color></b> you just learned
      about.
    - A <b><#E09500>truss</color></b> is made of connected structural members that
      work together to support the load.
    - For the structure to remain stable, those members need to work together as
      forces act on the bridge.
    - During the simulation, pay attention to how the connected members respond while
      the Vehicle cross.
    - Pay attention to how the members respond when the pedestrians cross the bridge.
    - Now that you've accepted the contract, follow the path to the <b><#E09500>Build
      Mode</color></b>.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - What are you waiting for?
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Excellent work, Engineer.
    - You've now built your first truss bridge.
    - You also learned how to erase. select, copy, and paste structural components.
    - Those tools will become useful when your designs become more complicated.
